# {{.ProjectName}}

A Go REST API built with Clean Architecture.

## Architecture

```bash
internal/
├── domain/                 # Layer 1: Enterprise Business Rules (innermost)
│   ├── entity/             # Business entities — pure Go structs, no framework tags
│   ├── identity/           # Authenticated principals + ctx plumbing
│   ├── security/           # Crypto port interfaces (PasswordHasher)
│   ├── user.go             # UserRepository interface + UserFilter
│   └── tx_manager.go       # TxManager port (WithinTx)
│
├── usecase/                # Layer 2: Application Business Rules
│   └── user/               # Service (Register, Login, Get, Update, Delete, List)
│
├── adapter/                # Layer 3: Interface Adapters
│   └── repository/
│       {{- if eq .Database "postgres"}}
│       ├── postgres/       # sqlc-backed UserRepository + TxManager + mapper
│       {{- end}}
│       {{- if eq .Database "mysql"}}
│       ├── mysql/          # sqlc-backed UserRepository + TxManager + mapper
│       {{- end}}
│       {{- if .HasRedis}}
│       └── redis/          # Cache-aside decorator over UserRepository
│       {{- end}}
│
├── transport/              # Inbound transport (HTTP/gRPC)
│   {{- if .HasHTTP}}
│   └── http/
│       ├── app.go          # Framework instance + middleware order + Registrar interface
│       ├── httpwriter/     # Framework-specific response envelope writer
│       ├── middleware/     # RequestID, Logging, Recovery, CORS, Locale, Auth
│       └── v1/user/        # Handler, Routes, DTOs, assembler
│   {{- end}}
│
├── app/                    # Entry-point glue (RunHTTPServer)
│
└── infrastructure/         # Layer 4: Frameworks & Drivers (outermost)
    ├── config/             # cleanenv + embed.FS (base/development/production)
    ├── database/           # {{.Database}} connection pool
    {{- if .HasRedis}}
    ├── cache/              # Redis client factory (single/sentinel/cluster)
    {{- end}}
    ├── jwt/                # TokenService (HS256 sign + verify)
    ├── logger/             # zerolog implementation of observability.Logger
    ├── security/           # bcrypt PasswordHasher implementation
    ├── server/             # HTTP server lifecycle (graceful shutdown)
    ├── tracing/            # OpenTelemetry provider + cleanup
    └── di/                 # {{if .UseWire}}Wire-generated{{else}}manual{{end}} dependency wiring
```

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Go {{.GoVersion}}+
  {{- if eq .Database "postgres"}}
- PostgreSQL 16+
  {{- end}}
  {{- if eq .Database "mysql"}}
- MySQL 8+
  {{- end}}
  {{- if .HasRedis}}
- Redis 7+
  {{- end}}
  {{- if .IncludeDocker}}
- Docker & Docker Compose
  {{- end}}

### Setup

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone {{.ModuleName}}
cd {{.ProjectName}}

# Copy environment variables
cp .env.example .env

# Generate a JWT secret (256-bit minimum) and add to .env
openssl rand -hex 32 | xargs -I {} sed -i.bak 's/^JWT_SECRET=.*/JWT_SECRET={}/' .env && rm .env.bak

# Install dependencies + run code generators (wire, sqlc)
go mod tidy
make gen
{{- if .IncludeDocker}}

# Start infrastructure (database, cache, etc.)
docker-compose up -d
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasDatabase}}

# Run migrations
make migrate-up
{{- end}}

# Run the server
go run main.go api
```

{{- if .HasHTTP}}

### API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint          | Auth   | Description                                |
| ------ | ----------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------ |
| POST   | /api/v1/login     | public | Exchange email/password for a bearer token |
| POST   | /api/v1/users     | public | Register a new user                        |
| GET    | /api/v1/users     | bearer | List users (paginated)                     |
| GET    | /api/v1/users/:id | bearer | Get user by ID                             |
| PUT    | /api/v1/users/:id | bearer | Update a user                              |
| DELETE | /api/v1/users/:id | bearer | Delete a user                              |
| GET    | /healthz          | public | Liveness check (always 200)                |
| GET    | /readyz           | public | Readiness check (200 / 503)                |

**Authenticated requests** carry `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>` where the token comes from `POST /api/v1/login`.

